---
code: effect-kind-disagreement
when-fires: a check's annotation kind disagrees with the effect-map kind for the same verb; the annotation wins. effect.rs (SPANLESS — mid-resolution, no leaf).
why: 204 §6 open seam: declared identity wins. The holes are typed: `{annotated}` is the kind the annotation declared and `{effect_map}` the kind the effect map holds.
---
-- book.sh --
#!/bin/sh
hork add nginx

-- hork.oracle.sh --
#!/usr/bin/env dorc-sh
# dorc-lang/v0.2
# The mark stands AHEAD of the bind, so the effect-map reads its kind off the coordinate while
# argparse reads the declared identity off the bind below it. The two disagree.
hork__predict() {
   verb=$1; shift
   case $verb in
      add)
         hork --query "$1" >/dev/null 2>&1 : sm.dorc.Service:"$1"@installed
         pkg : sm.dorc.Package = "$1"
         ;;
   esac
}

-- replay --
$ dorc plan --book=book.sh -o hork.oracle.sh
warning[effect-kind-disagreement]: this verb spells its kind two ways: the
identity bind declares `sm.dorc.Package` while the mark's own coordinate names
`sm.dorc.Service` -- Dorc files the fact under the declared `sm.dorc.Package`;
align the two spellings to clear this.

$ dorc-loom --this vars
case: effect-kind-disagreement
{{annotated}} = "sm.dorc.Package"
{{effect_map}} = "sm.dorc.Service"
